  "summary": "New methods resolve metastatic migration histories and heritable versus microenvironmental variation in tumors, alongside state-transition and communication frameworks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is inferring history, ancestry and inter-state relationships from static measurements. MACH2 enumerates all optimal metastatic migration histories from DNA sequencing and adds a clone-location parsimony criterion, characterizing the solution space rather than a single history. SOUR separates heritable lineage effects from spatial microenvironment effects on tumor cell expression in spatial lineage tracing data. A single-cell foundation model framework (Universal Cell Embedding) maps 22,161 significant bridges among 614 biological states, and SpaDAG learns spatially varying causal DAGs in spatial transcriptomics. A Nature Methods review curates 161 cell-cell communication methods. CellSieve (gene set selection) and TMCells (metacell construction) are supporting methods rather than lineage or trafficking inference. Compared with the previous emphasis on inter-tissue trafficking, the new items stress ambiguity in migration histories and disentangling inherited from environmental variation.",
